By the end of this lab, you will have a working prototype that can classify different types of motion and detect anomalies during the transportation of containers. This knowledge can serve as a basis for more advanced TinyML projects, particularly those involving vibration.



The XIAOML Kit comes with a built-in LSM6DS3TR-C 6-axis IMU sensor on the expansion board, so no external sensor connections are needed. This gives a reliable platform for motion-based machine learning applications.
The LSM6DS3TR-C combines a 3-axis accelerometer and 3-axis gyroscope in a single package, connected via I2C to the XIAO ESP32S3 at address 0x6A that provides:

Accelerometer ranges: ±2/±4/±8/±16 g (we use ±2g by default)
Gyroscope ranges: ±125/±250/±500/±1000/±2000 dps (we use ±250 dps by default)
Resolution: 16-bit ADC
Communication: I2C interface at address 0x6A
Power: Low power design


Coordinate System: The sensor operates within a right-handed coordinate system. When looking at the expansion board from the bottom (where you can see the IMU sensor with the point mark):

X-axis: Points to the right
Y-axis: Points forward (away from you)
Z-axis: Points upward (out of the board)



Since the XIAOML Kit comes pre-assembled with the expansion board, no additional hardware connections are required. The LSM6DS3TR-C IMU is already connected via I2C.
Already Connected:

LSM6DS3TR-C IMU → I2C (SDA/SCL) → XIAO ESP32S3
I2C Address: 0x6A
Power: 3.3V from XIAO ESP32S3

Required Library: You should have the library installed during the Setup. If not, install the Seeed Arduino LSM6DS3 library following the steps:

Open Arduino IDE Library Manager
Search for “LSM6DS3”
Install “Seeed Arduino LSM6DS3” by Seeed Studio
Important: Do NOT install “Arduino_LSM6DS3 by Arduino” - that’s for different boards!




